Subject: RackAI Project Update - Jun 4 2026

Work Completed

  *
Planned feature work for Uniphore MVP release was completed.
  *
Staging environment was validated and shared with Uniphore.
  *
To recap, this release to Uniphore added the following product features
     *
Model inference with NIM, in addition to open source vLLM.
     *
Optimization of these NIM models on vLLM based on our benchmarking, with the ability for the user to customize these further.
     *
Faster model start up with local cache of model weights.
     *
Autoscaling support of model deployments with scale to zero. LM cache and Routing are not included.
     *
Dataset management in the product for Fine Tuning jobs.
     *
Supervised Fine Tuning support
     *
LoRA adapter management. Ability to load/unload multiple LoRA adapters on a base model.
     *
UI and CLI support all of the above.
     *
AMD Integration (MVP - Inferencing as-a-service using AMD cards)
     *
GPU Accelerator Selection (MVP - Ability to select GPU to run workloads)

Work In Progress

  *
Certain bug fixes and improvements based on feedback from Uniphore.
  *
AMD cluster setup is underway.
  *
Support for selecting accelerator type during model deployment is being planned/discussed.

Work Planned

  *
Start implementation for the next milestone
     *
AMD FT and Inferencing as a service
     *
Autoscaling with LM cache and routing
     *
IAC
     *
Accelerator type support
  *
Knowledge sessions for RackAI deployment

Project Status
Green: Given the milestone delivery was completed, there are no major known risks at the start of the next milestone.



